        "ID": 0,
        "gui": {
          "x": "40.0",
          "y": "20.0",
          "w": "640"
        },
        "parms": "# poly — voice allocation\npoly hands each note a voice number, so a patch with several copies of a sound knows which copy plays it. Its arguments are the number of voices and whether to steal: poly 3 has three voices, and poly 3 1 also steals. The right inlet stores a velocity. A pitch on the left inlet takes the lowest free voice when that velocity is not 0, and frees the voice holding that pitch when it is 0. The velocity, the pitch and then the voice number go out, right to left.\nMax's poly has its overflow outlet only when it does not steal. Here the fourth outlet is always there, and stays silent while poly steals.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
