        "parms": "1. Click 100 to store a velocity, then 60, 64 and 67. Each note takes the lowest free voice: 1, 2 and 3. The boxes under poly 3 show voice, pitch and velocity. Now click 71: all three voices are busy, so poly 3 sends it out the overflow outlet as 71 100, and does not keep it.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 37": {
        "ID": 37,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "410.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "2. poly 3 1 steals instead: 71 takes the voice of 60, the note held longest. 60's release goes out first, then the new note on voice 1. pack puts voice, pitch and velocity in one list, route sends it to that voice's saw, and three saws play on the master bus. print writes every list to the log (Ctrl+J).",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 38": {
        "ID": 38,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "600.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "3. Click 0, then 64: both release voice 2, with velocity 0 and the same voice number. Click 71: poly 3 1 releases voice 1. poly 3 never gave 71 a voice, so its release follows the note out of the overflow outlet, as 71 0. Click stop to release every voice that still sounds.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
